---
import { verifyInstalled } from '../../scripts/horse-racing-release.mjs';
const { data } = await verifyInstalled();
const fixed = data.research.rows.find((row: { id: string }) => row.id === 'fixed');
const weekly = data.weekly.models.find(
  (model: { id: string }) => model.id === data.weekly.default_model,
);
const prospective = weekly.evaluation?.procedure || weekly.prospective;
const loss = prospective.probabilities?.methods?.calibrated;
const clinic = data.clinic_study;
const completedWeeks = [...(prospective.weekly || [])]
  .filter((week: {week: string; races: number}) => week.races > 0 && week.week.split('/')[1] < data.prospective.history_as_of)
  .sort((a: {week: string}, b: {week: string}) => b.week.localeCompare(a.week));
const latestWeek = completedWeeks[0];
const rate = (value: number) => `${(value * 100).toFixed(1)}%`;
const snapshot = new Date(data.exported_at).toLocaleString('en-GB', {
  timeZone: 'Asia/Seoul',
  dateStyle: 'medium',
  timeStyle: 'short',
});
---

<section class="horse-evidence" aria-labelledby="snapshot-evidence">
  <h2 id="snapshot-evidence">Snapshot evidence</h2>
  <p class="evidence-date">Updated {snapshot} KST · from the dashboard's saved data</p>
  <dl>
    <div>
      <dt>Historical winner hit rate</dt>
      <dd>{rate(fixed.metrics.win_hit)}</dd>
    </div>
    <div>
      <dt>Historical paid-place hit rate</dt>
      <dd>{rate(fixed.metrics.place_hit)}</dd>
    </div>
    <div>
      <dt>Historical scoring / payout races</dt>
      <dd>
        {data.research.scoring_races.toLocaleString('en')} /{' '}
        {data.research.payout_races.toLocaleString('en')}
      </dd>
    </div>
  </dl>
  <p>
    Fixed horse/jockey LSTM · {data.research.years.join('–')} · means across{' '}
    {data.research.seeds.length} seeds. Paid place means one selected horse finishes in a paying
    position.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>Weekly fixed-model replay:</strong> {rate(weekly.backtest.calibrated.winner_hit)} winner
    hits on {weekly.backtest.calibrated.races} held-out races. This is retrospective evidence,
    separate from the historical study.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>Registered prospective updating procedure:</strong> {prospective.recorded} captured /{' '}
    {prospective.evaluated} scored. Upcoming predictions are not scored as losses.
  </p>
  {latestWeek && <p><strong>Latest completed week:</strong> {latestWeek.first_date}–{latestWeek.last_date} ·
    {' '}{latestWeek.winner_credit}/{latestWeek.races} winners correct ({rate(latestWeek.winner_hit_rate)}).
    {prospective.metrics && ` Across the registered record: ${rate(prospective.metrics.winner_hit_rate)} winner hits.`}</p>}
  <p>
    <strong>Prospective probability scores:</strong>{' '}
    {loss
      ? `win log loss ${loss.log_loss.toFixed(4)}, Brier ${loss.brier.toFixed(4)} on ${loss.races} races`
      : 'pending verified outcomes'}
    . Lower scores indicate better probability forecasts.
  </p>
  {clinic && (
    <div class="clinic-forward-evidence">
      <h3>Clinic activity: forward study</h3>
      <p>{clinic.scored_races} races scored across {clinic.weeks} calendar week(s).
        {clinic.period && ` Scored dates: ${clinic.period.begin}–${clinic.period.end}.`}</p>
      {clinic.scored_races > 0 && (
        <div class="comparison-scroll" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Forward clinic comparison">
          <table>
            <thead><tr><th scope="col">Model / reference</th><th scope="col">Winner hit</th><th scope="col">Win log loss ↓</th><th scope="col">Brier ↓</th></tr></thead>
            <tbody>{clinic.rows.map((row: {id: string; label: string; metrics: {winner_hit: number; log_loss: number; brier: number}}) => (
              <tr><th scope="row">{row.label}</th><td>{rate(row.metrics.winner_hit)}</td><td>{row.metrics.log_loss.toFixed(4)}</td><td>{row.metrics.brier.toFixed(4)}</td></tr>
            ))}</tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
      )}
      <p>Preliminary research evidence. Historical clinic gains were withdrawn because
        the training archive depends on a later horse roster. Future inputs are timestamped;
        the training limitation remains. This candidate is separate from operational models.</p>
      <p>The uniform winner-hit rate is the expected random-pick rate for these fields.</p>
      <p>Weekly values are descriptive. The fixed final report is after {clinic.final_report_after},
        requiring {clinic.required_weeks} scored calendar weeks. No reliable gain or profit is established.</p>
    </div>
  )}
  <p>
    Models use scheduled batch retraining with rolling chronological windows. Future results
    evaluate the updating procedure and each exact version separately.
  </p>
  <p>
    Historical hit rates exceed the Korean 2025 paper's reported values on seven tasks; different
    datasets and validation prevent a direct superiority claim. All historical equal-stake pools
    lose money.
  </p>
  <a class="text-link" href="/demos/horse-racing/">
    Inspect models, forecasts and comparisons →
  </a>
</section>
<style>
  .comparison-scroll { overflow-x: auto; margin-block: 1rem; }
  table { border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; min-width: 32rem; }
  th, td { text-align: left; padding: 0.7rem; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--control-border); }
  .clinic-forward-evidence { margin-block: 2rem; }
  .horse-evidence {
    border-block: 1px solid var(--control-border);
    padding-block: 1.5rem;
    margin-bottom: 3rem;
  }
  .horse-evidence h2 {
    margin-top: 0;
  }
  .evidence-date {
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 0.85rem;
  }
  dl {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr));
    gap: 1.5rem;
    margin-block: 2rem;
  }
  dt {
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 0.85rem;
  }
  dd {
    font:
      600 1.5rem Sora,
      sans-serif;
    margin: 0.6rem 0 0;
    color: var(--ink);
  }
  @media (max-width: 600px) {
    dl {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      gap: 1rem;
    }
  }
</style>
